01:40:12.600 --> 01:40:16.260
SUPERVISOR MAHMOOD. >> COLLEAGUES IN THE SUMMER OF

01:40:18.734 --> 01:40:23.272
1966 THE TENDERLOIN MUCH LIKE TODAY WAS A CENTER OF CULTURE

01:40:23.272 --> 01:40:26.808
AND A HAVEN FOR PEOPLE MARGINALIZED BY SOCIETY.

01:40:26.808 --> 01:40:31.613
THE LOCATION OF GENE COMPTON'S CAFETERIA AT THE CORNER OF TURK

01:40:31.613 --> 01:40:34.616
AND TAYLOR WAS A PARTICULARLY IMPORTANT THIRD SPACE FOR THE

01:40:34.616 --> 01:40:37.219
TRANSGENDER COMMUNITY AT THE TIME.

01:40:37.219 --> 01:40:41.823
IN THE 1960S IN SAN FRANCISCO, CROSS-DRESSING WAS ILLEGAL

01:40:41.823 --> 01:40:45.827
AND TRANS WOMEN IN PARTICULAR WERE TARGETED BY STAFF AT THE

01:40:45.827 --> 01:40:49.980
CAFETERIA AND THE POLICE DEPARTMENT AT THE TIME.

01:40:49.980 --> 01:40:52.835
THESE TENSIONS CAME TO A HEAD ONE NIGHT IN AUGUST 1966 WHEN

01:40:52.835 --> 01:40:56.847
AFTER A TRANS WOMAN WAS ALMOST ARRESTED SHE FOUGHT BACK,

01:40:56.847 --> 01:41:00.184
GALVANIZED THE TRANS COMMUNITY AND THEIR ALLIES.

01:41:00.184 --> 01:41:04.188
>> THE VIOLENT CLASHES RECOGNIZES THE BEGINNING OF THE

01:41:04.188 --> 01:41:05.589
TRANSGENDER ACTIVISM MOVEMENT IN SAN FRANCISCO AND A

01:41:05.589 --> 01:41:09.593
PRECEDENT TO STONEWALL RIOT THREE YEARS LATER IN NEW YORK

01:41:09.593 --> 01:41:13.197
CITY. WHILE THE SITE IS RECOGNIZED ON

01:41:13.197 --> 01:41:16.266
THE NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES, THE FIRST SUCH

01:41:16.266 --> 01:41:17.668
PLACE IN THE NATION ASSOCIATED WITH THE TRANSGENDER RIGHTS

01:41:17.668 --> 01:41:21.338
MOVEMENT, THE LOCAL LANDMARKING HAS BEEN LIMITED TO THE FACADE

01:41:21.338 --> 01:41:27.144
OF THE FIRST FLOOR AND THE STREET IN FRONT OF TRANS

01:41:27.144 --> 01:41:28.545
ACTIVISTS AND COMMUNITY LEADERS HAVE BEEN CLEAR THAT THE

01:41:28.545 --> 01:41:32.820
LIMITED SCOPE OF THE LOCAL LANDMARKING IS UNACCEPTABLE.

01:41:32.820 --> 01:41:38.820
THE BUILDING AT 12121 21 TAYLOR AS A WHOLE REPRESENTS THE POWER

01:41:39.222 --> 01:41:40.624
OF THE TRANS MOVEMENT AND THE HISTORY OF RESISTANCE IN SAN

01:41:40.624 --> 01:41:43.360
FRANCISCO. >> THE BUILDING'S CURRENT USE

01:41:43.360 --> 01:41:47.164
HAS BEEN A POINT OF DIFFICULTY FOR THE TENDERLOIN COMMUNITY.

01:41:47.164 --> 01:41:50.300
IT OPERATES AS A TRANSITIONAL FACILITY UNDER FEDERAL

01:41:50.300 --> 01:41:54.237
CONTRACTS OWNED BY GEO GROUP, A PRIVATE PRISON COMPANY THAT

01:41:54.237 --> 01:41:55.639
CONTRACTS WITH ICE AND IS AN IMPORTANT ELEMENT OF THE

01:41:55.639 --> 01:41:58.390
NATION'S PRISON INDUSTRIAL COMPLEX.

01:41:58.442 --> 01:42:02.713
>> LAST YEAR I HELD A HEARING ON THE FACILITY AT TURK

01:42:02.713 --> 01:42:05.849
AND TAYLOR AFTER THE PASSING OF MELVIN BALOGUN WHO WAS IN THE

01:42:05.849 --> 01:42:07.117
GEO GROUP CUSTODY AT THE TIME OF HIS DEATH.

01:42:07.117 --> 01:42:10.120
WE HEARD FROM COMMUNITY MEMBERS THAT WERE FORMERLY RESIDENTS AT

01:42:10.120 --> 01:42:13.590
THE SITE ABOUT THE DEPLORABLE CONDITIONS AND AWFUL

01:42:13.590 --> 01:42:14.992
MISTREATMENT THAT THEY RECEIVED WITHIN THOSE WALLS.

01:42:14.992 --> 01:42:18.395
>> IT'S CLEAR THAT GEO GROUP IS OPERATING THIS BUILDING IN A

01:42:18.395 --> 01:42:21.998
WAY THAT IS AT ODDS WITH THE SPIRIT OF FREEDOM OF CIVIL

01:42:21.998 --> 01:42:25.468
RIGHTS THAT EMBODIES THE EVENTS THAT TOOK PLACE THERE 60 YEARS

01:42:25.468 --> 01:42:29.472
AGO AND POSES A THREAT TO THAT LEGACY.

01:42:29.472 --> 01:42:32.942
THAT'S WHY TODAY I'M INTRODUCING LEGISLATION

01:42:32.942 --> 01:42:36.480
LEGISLATION TO LANDMARK THE ENTIRE BUILDING THAT CONTAINS

01:42:36.480 --> 01:42:39.416
COMPTON CAFETERIA AS A SAN FRANCISCO ARTICLE TEN LANDMARK.

01:42:39.416 --> 01:42:43.286
>> THIS EFFORT WAS SHAPED IN CLOSE PARTNERSHIP WITH THE

01:42:43.286 --> 01:42:44.555
